Z||000000||b lo 0||07-25-2000||12:56 PM||||The throttle cable on my '85 GT seems either stretched or out of adjustment.  You have to press down the pedal about an inch before anything happens.  How (if you even can) adjust the tension on the throttle cable?  Also, the E-brake doesn't work at all.  I'm assuming the cable is busted, as there's no resistance.  And how do I replace the button on the end of the E-brake?  Do I have to replace the entire handle?  Thanks guys.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car||||reg||5
