Z||000003||triker||07-25-2000||05:12 PM||||I doubt your cable stretched. One of two things probably happened.  First it's possible the foot pedal is bent.  This can happen if you're trying to adjust the TVI linkage and it wont slip like it's supposed to.  The second and most likely is that the cable is hooked up wrong at the throttle body.  If you dont have cruise, the throttle cable could be in the cruise cable location which will leave your throttle cable loose. The throttle cable goes under the cam on the throttle body. Both of these have happened to me.  A previous owner screwed up the TVI adjuster and I bent the foot pedal trying to adjust it per the book and, after doing an engine replacement, I put the throttle cable in the wrong place.||||reg||1
